              "title": "No adjustment for potential confounders",
              "evidenceRefs": [
                "manuscript.md"
              ],
              "whyItMatters": "Observational associations may be confounded by variables that influence both treatment and outcome; the reported odds ratio may be biased even as an associative measure. Although the manuscript disclaims causality, readers may overinterpret the unadjusted estimate.",
              "actionableFix": "Either adjust the analysis for measured confounders (e.g., logistic regression) or explicitly discuss the potential confounders and the direction of bias. At minimum, include a statement about the unadjusted nature and list key unmeasured confounders.",
